<!-- ========== BENEFITS ========== -->
<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header fade-in">
            <span class="section-label">Why Work With Me</span>
            <h2>Share your ideas, and you&rsquo;ll reap all these benefits</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="benefits-grid">
            <div class="benefit-card fade-in">
                <div class="benefit-icon">&#9881;&#65039;</div>
                <h4>Architecture That Scales</h4>
                <p>From roadmap to execution, I deliver architectural clarity that grows with your business&mdash;without the full-time overhead.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-card fade-in">
                <div class="benefit-icon">&#128269;</div>
                <h4>Forensic Code Analysis</h4>
                <p>Unbiased, expert analysis of software systems for litigation, IP disputes, and contract breakdowns. When code is on trial, I make the technical case clear.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-card fade-in">
                <div class="benefit-icon">&#9889;</div>
                <h4>Fast, Focused Consulting</h4>
                <p>One hour. One problem. Real answers. Micro-consulting sessions to resolve architecture questions, performance issues, or critical forks in the road.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-card fade-in">
                <div class="benefit-icon">&#128101;</div>
                <h4>Team Mentorship</h4>
                <p>I don&rsquo;t just make decisions&mdash;I explain them. Your engineers grow as I guide, translating goals into scalable architecture while keeping leadership in the loop.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== SERVICES ========== -->
<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header fade-in">
            <span class="section-label">Services</span>
            <h2>Essential services for your organization</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="services-grid">
            <div class="service-card fade-in">
                <span class="service-num">01</span>
                <h3>Fractional Architect</h3>
                <p>High-impact software architecture when and how you need it. Technical leadership, platform strategy, and architectural clarity on a flexible schedule.</p>
                <a href="/Services/FractionalArchitect" class="service-link">Learn More <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="service-card fade-in">
                <span class="service-num">02</span>
                <h3>Expert Witness</h3>
                <p>Clear, objective software analysis when the stakes are high. In-depth technical analysis, expert reports, and courtroom-ready insights.</p>
                <a href="/Services/ExpertWitness" class="service-link">Learn More <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="service-card fade-in">
                <span class="service-num">03</span>
                <h3>Micro-Consulting</h3>
                <p>Fast, focused sessions to resolve architecture questions, performance issues, or critical forks in the road.</p>
                <a href="/Services/MicroConsulting" class="service-link">Learn More <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="service-card fade-in">
                <span class="service-num">04</span>
                <h3>Project-Based Contracts</h3>
                <p>I lead and execute focused architecture and modernization efforts with start-to-finish accountability. Clear deliverables, defined outcomes.</p>
                <a href="/Services/ProjectBased" class="service-link">Learn More <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="service-card fade-in">
                <span class="service-num">05</span>
                <h3>Retainer Services</h3>
                <p>Ongoing architecture support, available when your team needs clarity, feedback, or direction. Trusted guidance on call.</p>
                <a href="/Services/Retainer" class="service-link">Learn More <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="service-card fade-in">
                <span class="service-num">06</span>
                <h3>Advisory &amp; Board Roles</h3>
                <p>I advise leadership teams on platform evolution, scaling, technical risk, and innovation at the decision table.</p>
                <a href="/Services/Advisory" class="service-link">Learn More <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== PROCESS ========== -->
<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header fade-in">
            <span class="section-label">How I Work</span>
            <h2>A series of processes to achieve maximum results</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="process-steps">
            <div class="process-step fade-in">
                <div class="step-num">1</div>
                <h4>Discovery</h4>
                <p>We define your goals, pain points, and existing tech landscape in a focused kickoff session.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-step fade-in">
                <div class="step-num">2</div>
                <h4>Engagement</h4>
                <p>I embed with your team on a fractional basis, providing guidance, architecture reviews, and decision support.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-step fade-in">
                <div class="step-num">3</div>
                <h4>Execution</h4>
                <p>Clear deliverables and actionable recommendations&mdash;architecture interventions backed by experience and empathy.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="process-step fade-in">
                <div class="step-num">4</div>
                <h4>Iteration</h4>
                <p>As your needs evolve, I adjust my involvement. Stepping in deeper during transitions or staying high-level when stable.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== BLOG PREVIEW ========== -->
<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header fade-in">
            <span class="section-label">Blog &amp; Insights</span>
            <h2>Latest articles and insights</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="blog-grid">
            <a href="https://woodruff.dev/lease-pattern-in-net-a-lock-with-an-expiration-date-that-saves-your-data/" class="blog-card fade-in" target="_blank">
                <div class="blog-card-img">
                    <img src="/images/blog-lease-pattern.jpg" alt="Lease Pattern in .NET"
                         onerror="this.parentElement.innerHTML='<div style=\'display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:100%;font-size:2rem;color:#c9a96e\'>&#128221;</div>'" />
                </div>
                <div class="blog-card-body">
                    <div class="blog-card-meta">
                        <span class="blog-card-tag">Patterns</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Lease Pattern in .NET: A Lock With an Expiration Date</h3>
                    <p>Indefinite locks belong to a world where processes never crash and networks never split. A lease fixes that by putting a deadline on ownership.</p>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href="https://woodruff.dev/leader-election-in-net-picking-one-boss-without-creating-two/" class="blog-card fade-in" target="_blank">
                <div class="blog-card-img">
                    <img src="/images/blog-leader-election.jpg" alt="Leader Election in .NET"
                         onerror="this.parentElement.innerHTML='<div style=\'display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:100%;font-size:2rem;color:#c9a96e\'>&#128221;</div>'" />
                </div>
                <div class="blog-card-body">
                    <div class="blog-card-meta">
                        <span class="blog-card-tag">Patterns</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Leader Election in .NET: Picking One Boss Without Creating Two</h3>
                    <p>Leader election is the pattern that turns &ldquo;somebody should run this&rdquo; into &ldquo;exactly one node is allowed to run this.&rdquo;</p>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href="https://woodruff.dev/systems-thinking-meets-simplicity-first-a-decision-framework-for-software-architects/" class="blog-card fade-in" target="_blank">
                <div class="blog-card-img">
                    <img src="/images/blog-systems-thinking.jpg" alt="Systems Thinking Meets Simplicity-First"
                         onerror="this.parentElement.innerHTML='<div style=\'display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:100%;font-size:2rem;color:#c9a96e\'>&#128221;</div>'" />
                </div>
                <div class="blog-card-body">
                    <div class="blog-card-meta">
                        <span class="blog-card-tag">Simplicity-First</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Systems Thinking Meets Simplicity-First</h3>
                    <p>Our tools have never been more powerful, yet our systems have never felt more fragile. Two guiding philosophies emerge.</p>
                </div>
            </a>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align:center; margin-top: var(--space-lg)">
            <a href="/Blog" class="btn btn-outline">All Blog Posts <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

